<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MapMe's voice lives here.

  Three modes, and everything MapMe says is one of them:

    FUNCTIONAL   "Here's your route for today."
    ENCOURAGING  "Nice. That's your longest journey yet."
    REASSURING   "Couldn't save that. Let's try again."

  Rules:
    - Short. If it needs a semicolon, it needs rewriting.
    - Never blame the person. It is never "you denied permission".
    - Never robotic. No "operation successful", no "error occurred".
    - Personality shows up; it does not perform. Not every line is a joke.
    - Say what happens next, not what went wrong.

  The typography is chosen to match this: Bricolage Grotesque has warmth and a
  little irregularity, which is what a short friendly sentence needs. Copy and
  type are one decision, not two.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="app_name">MapMe</string>

    <!-- Onboarding. Three beats, one drawing, told from three distances. -->
